00:35:11.909 --> 00:35:13.855
I like you.


00:35:15.279 --> 00:35:17.759
Okay.


00:35:25.990 --> 00:35:32.635
Wow, I say I like you, and...
you immediately put out.


00:35:32.763 --> 00:35:34.834
If I'd have known it was that easy...


00:35:34.966 --> 00:35:37.469
- Shh, shh, shh.
- I would've just...


00:35:37.602 --> 00:35:38.774
Stop talking.


00:36:04.295 --> 00:36:05.501
Dr. Barron?


00:36:08.166 --> 00:36:12.012
Hi. Um , I'm here to, uh,


00:36:12.136 --> 00:36:15.015
pick up a file or something?


00:36:15.139 --> 00:36:18.313
Lisa is just decorative
when it comes to you, isn't she?


00:36:18.442 --> 00:36:22.151
Well, she's not exactly
high-tech security.


00:36:22.280 --> 00:36:24.419
How are you?


00:36:24.515 --> 00:36:26.358
- I'm all right.
- How was your day?


00:36:26.484 --> 00:36:27.963
It was good.


00:36:28.052 --> 00:36:29.793
Oh!


00:36:29.887 --> 00:36:32.766
- Mm mm mmm! Tonight.
- Mm-hmm?


00:36:32.857 --> 00:36:34.427
Dinner. Tablecloths.
All of the above.


00:36:34.525 --> 00:36:36.334
- God, you are obsessed...
- Finally, hmm?


00:36:36.427 --> 00:36:37.701
...with tablecloths.


00:36:37.828 --> 00:36:39.239
They are the marker of civilization.


00:36:39.363 --> 00:36:41.309
- Come on. You're coming.
- I'm not here tonight.


00:36:41.399 --> 00:36:43.640
I'm going to my parents'
for a long weekend.


00:36:43.734 --> 00:36:46.010
Oh, you're going to check
on their marital bliss, huh?


00:36:46.103 --> 00:36:47.343
Uh, sorry, this is just a little...


00:36:47.438 --> 00:36:48.849
- It's gonna be that much fun?
- No!


00:36:48.940 --> 00:36:50.749
- Nothing's that much fun.
- We go once every few months,


00:36:50.875 --> 00:36:53.253
we go to the beach,
and we play games.


00:36:53.377 --> 00:36:54.685
My dad loves playing games.


00:36:54.779 --> 00:36:56.087
It's really fun, actually.


00:36:56.214 --> 00:36:58.319
It does sound fun.
It sounds very fun.


00:36:58.416 --> 00:37:00.726
- I'd invite you.
- Would you?


00:37:00.851 --> 00:37:03.991
- Uh, yeah, it's just that my parents...
- Okay. No, I'd love to go.


00:37:04.088 --> 00:37:05.761
I have a little bit of an issue
inviting people...


00:37:05.890 --> 00:37:07.892
What? I was at their wedding!


00:37:08.025 --> 00:37:10.471
No one thought they would
ever see you again!


00:37:10.561 --> 00:37:11.869
- Oh, okay.
- Including me, so...


00:37:11.996 --> 00:37:12.974
Oh, wow, yeah. Just...


00:37:13.064 --> 00:37:15.567
That honesty thing you've got?
You can turn that down whenever.


00:37:15.700 --> 00:37:17.646
- No, truly.
- Seriously...


00:37:17.735 --> 00:37:19.214
I wanna give this a chance,


00:37:19.337 --> 00:37:24.218
and I don't want to bring in
the whole band yet.


00:37:24.342 --> 00:37:26.413
Is that okay?


00:37:27.445 --> 00:37:29.857
Yeah, it's fine. I have to work
this weekend, anyway.


00:37:29.947 --> 00:37:31.051
Then why are you bugging me?


00:37:31.182 --> 00:37:32.820
That's why I came,
to tell you I won't make it.


00:37:32.917 --> 00:37:35.397
- You're being obnoxious. Get out.
- Oh!


00:37:35.519 --> 00:37:37.396
- You're bugging me.
- No, you mean "attractive."


00:37:37.521 --> 00:37:39.592
- No, no, in English it's "attractive."
- I mean...


00:37:39.724 --> 00:37:40.964
- It's okay.
- Fuck you.


00:37:41.092 --> 00:37:44.266
Ow! Oh, God!
That's... never mind.


00:37:44.395 --> 00:37:46.136
- That gives me a great idea.
- Don't look it up.


00:37:51.702 --> 00:37:53.045
Hey, Bob!


00:37:53.137 --> 00:37:56.209
- Hey.
- What's up?


00:37:56.307 --> 00:37:59.880
Hi, sis, what's up?
You look lovely.


00:37:59.977 --> 00:38:03.481
You look strange, sis. Happy.


00:38:03.614 --> 00:38:05.992
So you're telling me
the blond guy is working?


00:38:06.117 --> 00:38:07.994
Jeez! You don't know how much.


00:38:08.119 --> 00:38:10.725
Thanks to me. And don't say "jeez"
in front of Bobby.


00:38:10.821 --> 00:38:12.767
It sounds too much like "Jesus".


00:38:31.776 --> 00:38:34.279
That car can only be Daniel's.


00:38:36.814 --> 00:38:39.090
- Three 8s.
- Oh, no!


00:38:40.117 --> 00:38:41.425
Three 6s.


00:38:41.519 --> 00:38:43.430
Hi!


00:38:43.521 --> 00:38:45.194
Can't we get rid of you?


00:38:45.323 --> 00:38:48.133
I miss your Mom.
What do you want me to do?


00:38:48.225 --> 00:38:49.829
Oh, such a big hug!


00:38:49.960 --> 00:38:51.166
If you want to play, join us now.


00:38:51.295 --> 00:38:52.330
Bobs, you're with me, okay?


00:38:52.463 --> 00:38:56.206
You're gonna help me get
all of Daniel's money, your uncle Daniel.


00:38:56.334 --> 00:38:59.008
I've been waiting many years
for this moment.


00:38:59.136 --> 00:39:00.479
So you've finally
learned to play well?


00:39:00.571 --> 00:39:02.209
I can play almost anything.


00:39:02.340 --> 00:39:06.049
Okay, let's go then.


00:39:06.177 --> 00:39:07.520
Come on.


00:39:07.645 --> 00:39:11.559
It's the International
Sock Skating Championship!


00:39:11.682 --> 00:39:13.787
Bobby wins!


00:39:23.461 --> 00:39:25.873
Up next...


00:39:25.996 --> 00:39:30.138
Clara... and Daniel!


00:39:31.702 --> 00:39:33.375
Clara wins!


00:39:33.504 --> 00:39:35.814
- Yeah! You suck!
- You're all cheaters!


00:39:43.047 --> 00:39:44.924
There you go.


00:39:45.049 --> 00:39:46.027
Thanks.


00:40:36.767 --> 00:40:39.611
Hey.


00:40:39.737 --> 00:40:41.614
Hey, what's up?


00:40:41.739 --> 00:40:43.184
Nothing.


00:40:43.274 --> 00:40:45.754
I was just coming to say good night.


00:40:45.843 --> 00:40:48.323
Oh. Good night.


00:40:50.781 --> 00:40:52.556
Okay.


00:41:13.304 --> 00:41:15.648
<i>This is Asher Grace.
Message, please.</i>


00:41:15.773 --> 00:41:18.583
Hey, Ash! So, I take it back.


00:41:18.676 --> 00:41:21.885
Please come.
Uh... I know you work tomorrow,


00:41:21.979 --> 00:41:25.426
but you can come the next day,
or whenever you can.


00:41:25.516 --> 00:41:29.328
Um, the address is saved
on your Waze, I think?


00:41:29.453 --> 00:41:31.729
We used your phone, right?
Those things got saved?


00:41:31.822 --> 00:41:35.599
Anyway, it's pretty much
a straight line from the border.


00:41:35.693 --> 00:41:40.005
Oh, and don't forget your passport.
If not, you're gonna stay here forever.


00:41:42.933 --> 00:41:46.745
Tsk. Okay.
Well, see you soon.


00:41:46.837 --> 00:41:48.441
Hopefully.


00:41:49.740 --> 00:41:52.050
You can call me
if, uh, you get lost, you know,


00:41:52.176 --> 00:41:53.382
or you can just...


00:41:53.511 --> 00:41:58.483
You can text me, as well. Okay! Bye.


00:42:06.023 --> 00:42:07.900
Morning, sunshine.


00:42:12.196 --> 00:42:13.539
Don't judge me.


00:42:14.865 --> 00:42:16.503
I didn't hear anybody.
I thought I was alone.


00:42:19.703 --> 00:42:21.979
They went to that beach
Francisco likes.


00:42:22.072 --> 00:42:23.949
No, what? Why didn't they
wake me up?


00:42:24.041 --> 00:42:26.521
I love the view on the way there.


00:42:30.514 --> 00:42:33.017
Did you really wipe off my drool?


00:42:34.652 --> 00:42:36.495
You want us to go?


00:42:38.923 --> 00:42:40.800
No... No! No!


00:42:40.891 --> 00:42:42.564
Hey, Claridad! That's enough!


00:43:00.578 --> 00:43:01.556
Oh...


00:43:07.051 --> 00:43:08.223
- What?
- Hop on.


00:43:08.319 --> 00:43:11.095
- No, I'm not crazy.
- Please.


00:43:11.221 --> 00:43:12.427
Hop on.


00:43:17.561 --> 00:43:19.973
- Ready?
- Ready.


00:43:22.633 --> 00:43:25.512
Aah! Ha ha!


00:43:28.872 --> 00:43:31.250
That's it! Yes...


00:43:38.482 --> 00:43:41.053
People don't come here
as much because it's not as hot,


00:43:41.151 --> 00:43:42.459
but I love it here.


00:43:42.586 --> 00:43:45.066
It reminds me of...


00:43:46.757 --> 00:43:49.033
- Of what?
- Well...


00:43:49.126 --> 00:43:50.298
Of family.


00:43:59.970 --> 00:44:02.007
You know what I've been
thinking about a lot?


00:44:02.139 --> 00:44:06.986
How to get dressed so it doesn't show
how much you care?


00:44:07.111 --> 00:44:09.955
Your first apartment in L.A.


00:44:13.884 --> 00:44:17.832
I mean, I've never been
as hot as I was there.


00:44:17.955 --> 00:44:21.164
Seriously, your sticky bedsheets?


00:44:21.291 --> 00:44:23.100
And I've lived in the Amazon!


00:44:25.996 --> 00:44:29.500
No, man... And the smell of dry soil.


00:44:29.633 --> 00:44:33.012
That place was a death trap.


00:44:33.137 --> 00:44:35.276
But you did escape with your life.


00:44:37.508 --> 00:44:39.510
Sometimes I don't even know why I left.


00:44:39.643 --> 00:44:41.418
Because you couldn't
stand in the shower.


00:44:41.512 --> 00:44:43.082
- No, silly...
- Yeah, okay, okay.


00:44:48.786 --> 00:44:52.165
You wanted to do more things,
didn't you? See other things.


00:44:52.289 --> 00:44:54.860
And don't tell me you regret it,
because I don't buy it.


00:44:54.992 --> 00:44:56.198
No, no, I don't regret it.


00:45:00.864 --> 00:45:03.367
But I'd have made you
come with me.


00:45:03.500 --> 00:45:06.174
"Made me"?
You didn't even ask me.


00:45:06.270 --> 00:45:08.841
You wouldn't have come.


00:45:08.939 --> 00:45:12.386
What? You would have?


00:45:12.509 --> 00:45:13.579
- No.
- No.


00:45:13.711 --> 00:45:16.055
- No, I wouldn't have.
- Right.


00:45:21.518 --> 00:45:23.191
What's the name of that kid you're seeing?


00:45:23.287 --> 00:45:24.527
Don't be an ass.


00:45:24.621 --> 00:45:26.692
- I'm just asking.
- Mm-hmm.


00:45:26.824 --> 00:45:28.201
- Yeah.
- You're asking like the ass you are.


00:45:28.325 --> 00:45:31.306
No, I'm just...
I don't... I don't see you with him.


00:45:31.395 --> 00:45:32.396
- You don't?
- No.


00:45:32.529 --> 00:45:35.032
He's not your type.


00:45:35.165 --> 00:45:37.577
- What do you know?
- But I do, I know you.


00:45:37.701 --> 00:45:40.910
People don't change.
He's not your type.


00:45:41.038 --> 00:45:42.210
I'm giving him a whirl.


00:45:42.339 --> 00:45:45.252
That's just it. He doesn't fit you.


00:45:45.375 --> 00:45:48.379
- He's nice and cute.
- Then he's a koala.


00:45:48.512 --> 00:45:50.651
You're seeing a koala.


00:45:52.716 --> 00:45:53.820
Shut up.


00:45:53.917 --> 00:45:57.057
He's easy to... deal with.


00:45:57.154 --> 00:45:59.293
He's easy to love.
He's easy to see.


00:45:59.423 --> 00:46:01.926
- "He's easy to see"?
- Yeah.


00:46:02.059 --> 00:46:03.732
Come on...


00:46:03.827 --> 00:46:07.468
- I'm done talking about it.
- Why?


00:46:07.598 --> 00:46:09.942
With you, I'm done talking about it
with you.


00:46:12.903 --> 00:46:14.405
Okay.


00:46:16.840 --> 00:46:19.286
- What about you?
- What?


00:46:19.409 --> 00:46:22.947
What? Aren't you old enough to date?


00:46:23.080 --> 00:46:25.617
- I'm just saying.
- And I believe I am.


00:46:25.749 --> 00:46:28.889
You've not found anyone...


00:46:28.986 --> 00:46:31.557
I don't know, interesting enough
to be your first wife?


00:46:31.655 --> 00:46:32.929
No.


00:46:33.056 --> 00:46:35.093
- Nobody?
- No.


00:46:35.225 --> 00:46:36.966
But then you're dating that koala.


00:46:40.264 --> 00:46:43.473
Besides, you already
were my first wife.


00:46:43.600 --> 00:46:48.572
I don't remember you
being my lawfully anything.


00:46:48.672 --> 00:46:50.709
What's a wife?
It's a home, a family...


00:46:55.445 --> 00:46:57.823
- You're my first home.
- Exactly.


00:46:57.948 --> 00:46:59.359
- Mm-hmm, exactly.
- Yeah.


00:46:59.483 --> 00:47:01.963
We always leave our first home.


00:47:07.124 --> 00:47:09.365
Come on, chatterbox, let's go.


00:47:10.627 --> 00:47:12.538
- Hey!
- Hey!


00:47:12.663 --> 00:47:15.269
About time!


00:47:15.365 --> 00:47:18.642
How was your morning?


00:47:18.735 --> 00:47:20.806
- Huh?
- Just fine.


00:47:20.904 --> 00:47:22.042
How fine?


00:47:22.172 --> 00:47:24.709
Did you and Daniel talk?


00:47:24.842 --> 00:47:26.480
Why's he here, Mom?


00:47:26.577 --> 00:47:28.022
Because he's back.


00:47:28.145 --> 00:47:30.989
No, he's back in Los Angeles.
Why is he <i>here?</i>


00:47:31.114 --> 00:47:32.855
He invited himself.
Why would that be?


00:47:32.983 --> 00:47:35.691
Mom... stop playing Cupid.


00:47:35.819 --> 00:47:39.699
But why? I really love seeing him.


00:47:39.823 --> 00:47:44.272
When I hug him, I feel
like I'm hugging Clara ten years ago.


00:47:44.361 --> 00:47:47.137
He represents a time in her life.


00:47:47.231 --> 00:47:49.643
Which time? *The "I'm happy
and in love" time?


00:47:49.733 --> 00:47:52.839
Or the "I'll cry for months
because he left" time?


00:47:55.739 --> 00:47:58.345
I can't forget...


00:47:59.710 --> 00:48:02.554
the way Daniel used to make you laugh.


00:48:02.679 --> 00:48:05.592
The house would shake.


00:48:05.716 --> 00:48:07.593
It was a laughter that made you fly.


00:48:07.718 --> 00:48:09.254
That's true...


00:48:09.386 --> 00:48:10.694
Fly they did.


00:48:12.222 --> 00:48:13.895
Oh!


00:48:14.024 --> 00:48:16.595
- My coffee!
- Abby!


00:48:38.582 --> 00:48:40.323
The face started melting off.


00:49:53.256 --> 00:49:56.430
There's so much talent here!


00:49:56.526 --> 00:49:59.336
<i>Ay, ay, ay!</i>


00:50:24.021 --> 00:50:26.501
Sorry.


00:51:05.328 --> 00:51:06.807
- Hey...
- Mm?


00:51:08.865 --> 00:51:12.779
Many things have changed
since you last saw me naked.


00:51:12.903 --> 00:51:14.348
I know.


00:51:14.438 --> 00:51:17.544
No, I don't mean in life,
I mean like this.


00:51:17.641 --> 00:51:19.245
Check it out.


00:51:21.645 --> 00:51:23.090
You wanna see my washboard?


00:51:23.213 --> 00:51:25.887
- Oh, yeah? Show me...
- Check 'em out.


00:51:30.053 --> 00:51:32.533
That's horrible...


00:51:45.268 --> 00:51:47.748
Mm...


00:52:08.458 --> 00:52:10.096
Shh...


00:52:49.432 --> 00:52:52.345
You see? That's what happens.


00:52:59.643 --> 00:53:02.146
She's your girlfriend. She's...


00:53:04.848 --> 00:53:07.021
- No, that's enough!
- Give me a sec, hold on.


00:53:07.150 --> 00:53:09.357
Imagine you're standing up.


00:53:09.486 --> 00:53:12.524
You've no idea, Clara, what it felt like.


00:53:12.656 --> 00:53:14.067
You can't imagine...


00:53:14.191 --> 00:53:17.661
And suddenly you're going that way and...


00:53:17.761 --> 00:53:19.707
No, enough, yeah.


00:53:28.271 --> 00:53:32.515
I don't want to love you.
Why do I still love you?


00:53:34.511 --> 00:53:37.185
You're right.
There's no other way.


00:53:41.051 --> 00:53:43.759
What about you?


00:53:43.887 --> 00:53:45.628
Me neither.


00:53:47.524 --> 00:53:50.971
We'll always love each other.


00:53:51.061 --> 00:53:53.337
Even when we're apart.
There's no way around it.


00:54:02.539 --> 00:54:06.681
Loving each other or being apart?


00:54:32.836 --> 00:54:33.814
Morning.


00:54:33.937 --> 00:54:36.247
Hey...


00:54:36.339 --> 00:54:38.478
Why are you up so early?


00:54:38.608 --> 00:54:40.315
Max snores.


00:54:55.759 --> 00:55:00.299
Max? Wake up.


00:55:00.430 --> 00:55:02.410
Hey, wake up.


00:55:02.499 --> 00:55:05.480
Let's have sex.


00:55:05.602 --> 00:55:07.047
Max?


00:55:07.137 --> 00:55:09.879
Sex. Come on.


00:55:09.973 --> 00:55:11.316
Hmm.


00:55:18.181 --> 00:55:20.161
What? No, wait.
Yeah, yeah.


00:55:20.283 --> 00:55:21.626
- Too late!
- Yeah! Let's do it.


00:55:22.719 --> 00:55:25.199
Oh, man.


00:55:39.035 --> 00:55:42.039
Oh, no...


00:55:45.141 --> 00:55:46.518
<i>Clara, hi. Um...</i>


00:55:46.643 --> 00:55:51.251
<i>Just letting you know I got your message,
and I'll be there tonight, okay?</i>


00:55:51.348 --> 00:55:53.191
<i>See you soon.</i>


00:55:55.452 --> 00:55:57.693
Hi, Lisa, it's Dr. Barron.
Could you do me a favor?


00:55:57.821 --> 00:55:59.994
Could you please call Lily
and Beto Alvarez


00:56:00.123 --> 00:56:04.265
and tell them that I <i>can</i>
see them today, after all?


00:56:04.361 --> 00:56:08.207
Yes, I'll be there in three hours. Okay.


00:56:08.331 --> 00:56:11.437
Has he not hurt you enough?
Do you want him to kill you?


00:56:11.534 --> 00:56:14.208
Let's not be so nosy or overdramatic.


00:56:14.337 --> 00:56:16.214
What are you wearing?


00:56:16.339 --> 00:56:19.548
I've a patient in Los Angeles.


00:56:21.444 --> 00:56:24.186
He was gone by the time I woke up.


00:56:24.280 --> 00:56:25.418
Yeah, to the kitchen.


00:56:25.548 --> 00:56:28.757
Whatever. I need to leave.
I need to breathe.


00:56:31.955 --> 00:56:33.866
And I called Asher
and I told him to come,


00:56:33.957 --> 00:56:36.233
but he's not picking up
and I need to go intercept him.


00:56:36.359 --> 00:56:38.930
You called Asher here
with Daniel in the room?


00:56:39.062 --> 00:56:40.700
- Before that.
- What do you mean, before?


00:56:40.797 --> 00:56:42.401
Daniel has been here
since before we arrived.


00:56:42.532 --> 00:56:45.103
Before... last night.


00:56:45.235 --> 00:56:47.237
I called him to neutralize Daniel.


00:56:47.370 --> 00:56:49.611
Asher is a great Daniel neutralizer.


00:56:49.739 --> 00:56:51.810
Right, and who will neutralize him?


00:56:51.908 --> 00:56:54.149
I'll be back tonight.


00:56:54.244 --> 00:56:55.746
Alone or with the neutralizer?


00:56:55.879 --> 00:56:57.324
I don't know.


00:56:59.282 --> 00:57:00.886
I can deal, Abby. I promise.


00:57:01.017 --> 00:57:03.554
I just have to hold on until he leaves
again, which I'm sure will be soon.


00:57:03.686 --> 00:57:08.192
But I need reinforcements.
I'm going out... for reinforcements.


00:57:10.260 --> 00:57:11.898
And I need your car.


00:57:29.846 --> 00:57:33.623
Hi. I'm Dr. Barron.
I'm looking for Dr. Grace.


00:57:33.750 --> 00:57:36.287
He's a resident down here.


00:57:36.419 --> 00:57:37.921
I know who he is.
He's not here.


00:57:38.021 --> 00:57:40.399
Um, are you sure?
'Cause he said he would be...


00:57:40.490 --> 00:57:44.597
I'm sure. He asked for the shift off,
annoyed the crap out of me.


00:57:44.694 --> 00:57:47.334
Okay.


00:57:51.601 --> 00:57:53.911
<i>This is Asher Grace.
Message, please.</i>


00:57:55.472 --> 00:57:56.746
Mm...


00:57:58.141 --> 00:58:01.554
Well... Everything looks fine.


00:58:01.644 --> 00:58:04.488
It seems Clark's
been having a good time.


00:58:04.614 --> 00:58:06.958
We've been working out together.


00:58:07.083 --> 00:58:09.757
- Beto and you?
- No, Clark and me.


00:58:11.788 --> 00:58:13.768
Is it okay if they work out?


00:58:13.857 --> 00:58:18.738
Of course, yes, as long as it's not high
impact and she's not sore at the end,


00:58:18.828 --> 00:58:20.603
she can work out
as much as she wants.


00:58:20.697 --> 00:58:21.903
Cool, cool.


00:58:21.998 --> 00:58:24.342
See, Beto doesn't like to work out.


00:58:24.467 --> 00:58:28.381
Not that it shows...
but his belly's as big as mine,


00:58:28.505 --> 00:58:29.711
only he has no excuse.


00:58:29.839 --> 00:58:32.342
Between that and the hair, well...


00:58:34.143 --> 00:58:37.124
You know what, Lily?
It's none of my business, but...


00:58:37.213 --> 00:58:40.888
you're having a child with this man.
You shouldn't talk to him that way.


00:58:41.017 --> 00:58:43.520
And Beto, stop rubbing on that shirt.


00:58:43.653 --> 00:58:45.564
You won't clean it now. Rather...


00:58:47.991 --> 00:58:50.699
I've known you for a long time.
You're very nice people.


00:58:50.827 --> 00:58:52.500
You once loved
each other very much


00:58:52.595 --> 00:58:55.007
and you had the potential
to be good parents,


00:58:55.098 --> 00:58:58.705
but if you keep on being this idiotic,
which, by the way, you're great at,


00:58:58.835 --> 00:59:02.874
the only potential you have
is that of ruining your baby's life,


00:59:03.006 --> 00:59:05.452
and it's not his fault if his parents
can't stand each other.


00:59:05.542 --> 00:59:08.284
So you either make up or break up,


00:59:08.378 --> 00:59:11.188
because bringing a baby
into this situation...


00:59:11.314 --> 00:59:12.292
Mm-mm.


00:59:12.382 --> 00:59:14.521
It's not right, okay?


00:59:14.651 --> 00:59:16.221
Okay?


00:59:18.521 --> 00:59:21.058
Okay, okay.


00:59:21.190 --> 00:59:22.396
Yeah.


00:59:24.694 --> 00:59:26.196
Cool beans.


00:59:28.631 --> 00:59:31.908
Today's appointment is on me.


00:59:32.035 --> 00:59:33.241
Why not?


00:59:35.138 --> 00:59:36.913
Watch it, idiot!


00:59:37.040 --> 00:59:38.280
- Sorry!
- Asher!


00:59:38.408 --> 00:59:40.388
Clara. What are you doing here?


00:59:40.476 --> 00:59:42.615
I'm literally on my way
to your parents' house.


00:59:42.745 --> 00:59:45.453
I , uh, had a patient,
and I was looking for you.


00:59:45.582 --> 00:59:47.084
But you're not answering your phone,


00:59:47.216 --> 00:59:49.025
and you're not at work
when you say you will be, so...


00:59:49.118 --> 00:59:50.119
Clara, I can explain.


00:59:50.253 --> 00:59:52.130
Uh, don't.


00:59:52.255 --> 00:59:54.758
Uh, I gotta go. I have to go
to my parents' for dinner.


00:59:54.891 --> 00:59:58.100
- Yeah, well, let's go.
- Uh, no. No.


00:59:58.227 --> 01:00:00.571
Are you uninviting me
to the family weekend?


01:00:00.697 --> 01:00:01.937
Yes.


01:00:02.065 --> 01:00:03.169
Uh-uh.


01:00:03.266 --> 01:00:05.906
- You don't want to come, trust me.
- I do. I do.


01:00:06.035 --> 01:00:08.606
- Asher.
- Clara.


01:00:09.806 --> 01:00:11.786
I do.


01:00:11.908 --> 01:00:13.012
Pfft.


01:00:13.109 --> 01:00:16.056
Whatever it is, I'm up for it.


01:00:25.488 --> 01:00:27.058
Hey, I , uh...


01:00:27.156 --> 01:00:30.968
I want to explain where I've been
the past couple of days,


01:00:31.094 --> 01:00:32.471
and why I wasn't answering my phone.


01:00:32.595 --> 01:00:34.802
- No, that's okay.
- No, no, no, I want to.


01:00:34.931 --> 01:00:36.433
Um...


01:00:36.532 --> 01:00:39.513
So, my wife, Liz, she...


01:00:39.636 --> 01:00:40.671
Your wife?


01:00:40.803 --> 01:00:42.009
Well, see...


01:00:42.138 --> 01:00:43.515
Your wife? Oh, my God.


01:00:43.640 --> 01:00:46.314
Oh, no, no, no. It's not like that.


01:00:46.442 --> 01:00:48.649
- No, she's not around or anything.
- Oh, my God, I'm such an idiot.


01:00:48.778 --> 01:00:51.019
- No, she's not...
- What do you mean, she's not around?


01:00:51.147 --> 01:00:54.788
She's dead, Clara. She died.


01:00:59.989 --> 01:01:01.593
My God, Asher, I'm so sorry.


01:01:01.691 --> 01:01:04.934
It's... you...


01:01:05.028 --> 01:01:08.441
It was, uh, two years ago yesterday.


01:01:11.701 --> 01:01:14.272
And I forgot.


01:01:15.838 --> 01:01:17.146
You forgot?


01:01:17.273 --> 01:01:20.982
The, uh, the date.


01:01:21.110 --> 01:01:24.182
Caught me by surprise.
I just... I've been...


01:01:24.313 --> 01:01:27.817
Look, I wanted to apologize
because I was supposed to be at work,


01:01:27.950 --> 01:01:29.952
and I know I wasn't, and I'm sorry.


01:01:30.053 --> 01:01:33.967
Yeah, damn, yeah, yeah.
No. Okay.


01:01:38.928 --> 01:01:41.909
You're a 28-year-old widower?


01:01:42.031 --> 01:01:43.339
Yeah.


01:01:43.433 --> 01:01:47.677
Yeah, I was, uh, 19 when we got married.


01:01:49.272 --> 01:01:50.842
Why?


01:01:52.842 --> 01:01:54.412
I was in love.


01:01:56.846 --> 01:01:59.087
Yeah, well...


01:01:59.215 --> 01:02:02.526
I was in love when I was 19,
and I didn't get married.


01:02:04.353 --> 01:02:06.458
Well, I did.


01:02:11.894 --> 01:02:14.204
Oh, my God, I'm such a horrible person.


01:02:14.330 --> 01:02:16.810
What? Why?


01:02:21.938 --> 01:02:24.179
Daniel is at my parents' house
right now.


01:02:24.273 --> 01:02:25.650
Yeah, of course he is.


01:02:32.682 --> 01:02:34.389
What do you mean,
"Of course he is"?


01:02:34.484 --> 01:02:37.556
Well, you obviously needed
some form of extreme backup


01:02:37.653 --> 01:02:40.532
when you changed your mind
about inviting me.


01:02:40.623 --> 01:02:41.727
Come on!


01:02:45.394 --> 01:02:47.806
Are we both completely
screwed up, Ash?


01:02:47.930 --> 01:02:50.740
Both of...? No, <i>you</i> are.
That's for certain.


01:02:50.833 --> 01:02:53.313
Me, I'm a respectable widower,
thank you very much.


01:02:53.436 --> 01:02:54.881
Right, you do have that
going for you.


01:02:54.971 --> 01:02:57.815
Yeah.


01:03:07.083 --> 01:03:08.619
Bring on the ex, hmm?


01:03:12.488 --> 01:03:14.525
Are you allowed to scold your patients


01:03:14.624 --> 01:03:16.968
like they were your spoiled students?


01:03:17.093 --> 01:03:20.631
No... But I'd had it.


01:03:20.763 --> 01:03:24.540
Right, but you are their doctor.
They have to trust you.


01:03:24.634 --> 01:03:26.705
Asher agrees with me.


01:03:26.803 --> 01:03:28.976
I know, I do.


01:03:29.105 --> 01:03:31.642
Okay... they do trust her, though.


01:03:31.774 --> 01:03:33.549
That's why it was great you told them.


01:03:33.643 --> 01:03:35.645
I'm sorry, it's just...
Okay...


01:03:35.778 --> 01:03:37.985
People often don't know
what they want, right?


01:03:38.114 --> 01:03:40.253
And they go through life
forming couples,


01:03:40.349 --> 01:03:42.158
just to see if they can save themselves.


01:03:42.285 --> 01:03:44.026
I'm sorry, it doesn't work like that.


01:03:44.153 --> 01:03:48.431
It was great someone they trust
told them what life is like.


01:03:48.524 --> 01:03:51.437
Yeah, I overreached, but they deserved it.
You should see them.


01:03:51.527 --> 01:03:53.598
You guys should see them.
They hate each other.


01:03:53.696 --> 01:03:56.176
And I've known them for a while
and they used to be happy.


01:03:56.299 --> 01:03:59.439
Then they chose the moment when their
marriage went to shit to have a baby.


01:03:59.535 --> 01:04:01.811
It's just...


01:04:01.904 --> 01:04:03.315
It's mean.


01:04:03.406 --> 01:04:05.443
Exactly!


01:04:05.541 --> 01:04:08.317
It's mean to have a go
at someone you don't know


01:04:08.444 --> 01:04:10.685
about things you don't understand.


01:04:10.813 --> 01:04:12.087
Well, yeah, but no.


01:04:12.181 --> 01:04:17.028
Ahem. I mean, it takes two seconds to see
if a couple is happy, you know,


01:04:17.153 --> 01:04:19.861
if they belong together,
or if they just settled, right?


01:04:19.989 --> 01:04:21.332
Have a taste?


01:04:21.457 --> 01:04:23.869
I mean, look in this room.


01:04:23.993 --> 01:04:25.768
No? Look at Francisco and Eva.


01:04:25.862 --> 01:04:28.206
It's obvious they belong together.


01:04:28.331 --> 01:04:31.335
Obvious who's happy and who's not.


01:04:32.835 --> 01:04:34.212
Here you go.


01:04:41.344 --> 01:04:45.224
Yeah, the mole's, um, it's great. Ahem.


01:04:45.348 --> 01:04:48.386
Where did you, uh...
How'd you learn how to make it?


01:04:48.517 --> 01:04:50.758
Oh, this old lady
in Oaxaca taught me.


01:04:50.887 --> 01:04:55.393
We were setting up sort of like a pirate
health station in the Sierra.


01:04:55.524 --> 01:04:57.197
Thanks.


01:05:01.464 --> 01:05:04.240
He's not neutralizing him , is he?


01:05:04.367 --> 01:05:05.937
Maybe you can have
for a threesome later.


01:05:06.068 --> 01:05:08.048
The trick is just to let
the last chili float.


01:05:08.137 --> 01:05:09.377
It will be great with the chocolate,


01:05:09.472 --> 01:05:11.850
so then you get the hotness
without the acidity.


01:05:11.941 --> 01:05:13.079
You get the punch.


01:05:13.209 --> 01:05:15.314
Actually, if you grind it all up before,


01:05:15.411 --> 01:05:18.255
and then let it meld together,
it makes it smoother.


01:05:18.381 --> 01:05:20.657
But it's probably a bit
too late for that now, I guess.


01:05:20.750 --> 01:05:22.320
Oh, is that right?


01:05:22.418 --> 01:05:25.729
Oh, sorry, one of my patients
is the son of a Mexican chef.


01:05:25.855 --> 01:05:28.597
Oh, 'cause I thought your Mexican
grandmother Jacinta


01:05:28.724 --> 01:05:29.930
taught you how to make mole.


01:05:30.059 --> 01:05:31.902
She's not real, Daniel.
Clara made her up.


01:05:32.028 --> 01:05:34.736
We can't all be as authentically Mexican
as you, champ.


01:05:34.864 --> 01:05:38.505
Or as randomly bicultural
as you, right, "champ"?


01:05:38.601 --> 01:05:40.672
All right, all right,
please, that's enough.


01:05:42.738 --> 01:05:44.547
Daniel, thank you for dinner,


01:05:44.640 --> 01:05:47.484
but I think it's too late for mole,
isn't it?


01:05:47.610 --> 01:05:49.112
Let's all go to bed, please.


01:05:51.147 --> 01:05:52.421
Clara.


01:05:54.083 --> 01:05:55.289
Good night.


01:05:55.418 --> 01:05:58.729
Good night. Good night.


01:06:03.626 --> 01:06:05.503
I'm sorry he's being a dick.


01:06:05.628 --> 01:06:07.630
Don't. Don't, please.


01:06:07.763 --> 01:06:10.505
What? I'm sorry.


01:06:10.633 --> 01:06:12.635
Uh, I gotta say, Clara...


01:06:12.768 --> 01:06:16.113
This time I feel like
he has a valid reason for it.


01:06:16.238 --> 01:06:17.216
Ash, I...


01:06:17.306 --> 01:06:19.980
Don't... I'm not asking for details.


01:06:20.109 --> 01:06:23.249
I just, um...


01:06:23.346 --> 01:06:25.656
I've gotta say it.


01:06:45.334 --> 01:06:46.836
Good morning, Asher.


01:06:46.969 --> 01:06:47.970
Morning.


01:06:48.070 --> 01:06:50.016
Do you want to play?


01:06:50.139 --> 01:06:52.619
Uh, sure. Yeah.


01:06:58.814 --> 01:07:00.725
- Deal him in, Francisco.
- Thank you.


01:07:00.850 --> 01:07:04.491
Hey, listen, bro, I'm really sorry
about last night.


01:07:04.587 --> 01:07:07.363
It got kind of weird. I'm sorry.


01:07:07.490 --> 01:07:10.471
It's fine.


01:07:14.330 --> 01:07:16.207
What's going on?


01:07:16.332 --> 01:07:18.812
You can still get in. Come on.


01:07:26.308 --> 01:07:29.346
All arguments in this house
are solved with a card game,


01:07:29.478 --> 01:07:30.548
especially a poker game.


01:07:30.679 --> 01:07:34.684
I should probably let you all know
I'm not very good.


01:07:34.817 --> 01:07:36.228
Join the club.


01:07:36.352 --> 01:07:38.229
It's people lying.


01:07:38.354 --> 01:07:40.891
You know, that's what poker's all about.


01:07:41.023 --> 01:07:45.563
So that's why some of the members
of this family excel at it, hmm?


01:07:45.694 --> 01:07:48.538
Are you good at telling
when someone's lying to you, Ash?


01:07:48.631 --> 01:07:50.110
Keeping stuff from you?


01:07:50.232 --> 01:07:53.213
Good enough to know you're not talking
about poker anymore, sure.


01:07:53.302 --> 01:07:55.612
Hey, smart man.


01:07:55.738 --> 01:07:58.412
You still know how to pick 'em, Clara.


01:07:59.909 --> 01:08:02.583
Daniel, come with me a sec, please?


01:08:02.711 --> 01:08:05.851
I'll go with you anywhere you want
for as long as you want.


01:08:07.616 --> 01:08:08.856
Excuse me.


01:08:14.423 --> 01:08:16.130
Okay, I want two.


01:08:16.258 --> 01:08:18.260
Are you having fun?


01:08:18.394 --> 01:08:19.429
- And you?
- You having a blast?


01:08:19.562 --> 01:08:22.065
Yeah, I am.
Did you have a blast last night?


01:08:23.632 --> 01:08:25.236
How old are you?


01:08:25.367 --> 01:08:27.404
- Asher?
- You're like an adolescent!


01:08:27.536 --> 01:08:30.073
You're behaving like a child. Stop it!


01:08:30.206 --> 01:08:31.446
- Stop what?
- I mean, no, no.


01:08:31.574 --> 01:08:32.780
I can't do this with you!


01:08:35.077 --> 01:08:36.454
Because I wasn't thinking straight.


01:08:36.579 --> 01:08:38.718
You get inside my head
and I can't think straight.


01:08:41.450 --> 01:08:43.191
We're doing this?
We're gonna do this?


01:08:43.285 --> 01:08:44.457
We're doing this. Here we go.


01:08:44.587 --> 01:08:47.431
I don't want to wake up alone
feeling like an idiot ever again


01:08:47.556 --> 01:08:50.127
if you can't even stay
and sleep next to me.


01:08:50.259 --> 01:08:53.832
This can't be.
You've been leaving all your life.


01:08:53.963 --> 01:08:55.567
- So go away!
- I'm here!


01:08:55.664 --> 01:08:57.439
I've not left. I'm here, okay?


01:08:57.533 --> 01:08:59.240
And if I leave, I'm leaving with you.


01:08:59.335 --> 01:09:02.441
- I don't believe you.
- You don't believe me?


01:09:02.538 --> 01:09:04.313
Why can't you believe, Clara,


01:09:04.440 --> 01:09:06.317
that people can fall in love
and stay together


01:09:06.442 --> 01:09:08.319
if you see it every damn day?


01:09:08.444 --> 01:09:09.980
No, but I do believe it.


01:09:10.112 --> 01:09:12.114
Other people. Fortunate people.


01:09:12.214 --> 01:09:15.127
I somehow pissed off fate and got you.


01:09:15.217 --> 01:09:17.322
Yeah, I've seen it triumph once.


01:09:17.453 --> 01:09:18.864
The rest of the time, it's failed.


01:09:18.988 --> 01:09:20.558
I lost count of the women
who come to my office,


01:09:20.656 --> 01:09:22.397
crying because they can
no longer stand the husband


01:09:22.491 --> 01:09:24.903
I saw them long for two years earlier.


01:09:24.994 --> 01:09:26.940
And there's the men who come in
with their menopausal wives,


01:09:27.029 --> 01:09:28.599
whom they dump for teenagers.


01:09:28.697 --> 01:09:31.405
And we're all the same, right?
I'm like them.


01:09:31.500 --> 01:09:33.480
No, you're worse.
You didn't even get to start.


01:09:33.602 --> 01:09:35.240
You didn't even show up.


01:09:37.973 --> 01:09:40.317
- Look, I love you.
- You love me?


01:09:40.442 --> 01:09:42.353
Right, you love me just like you did
the first time around,


01:09:42.478 --> 01:09:43.513
and we know it wasn't very much.


01:09:43.646 --> 01:09:45.922
Oh, Clara.


01:09:46.015 --> 01:09:47.926
What are you doing with that kid?


01:09:48.017 --> 01:09:49.428
- I like him.
- Yeah, okay.


01:09:49.518 --> 01:09:51.498
You like him like you like warm water.


01:09:51.587 --> 01:09:54.363
Please don't tell me
you're with him because it's easy,


01:09:54.490 --> 01:09:55.560
because I swear, if you do...


01:09:55.691 --> 01:09:57.864
I'll say whatever
I feel like saying, okay?


01:09:57.993 --> 01:10:01.372
As many times as I want to say it,
because this is all your fault.


01:10:01.497 --> 01:10:02.976
This is all your fault!


01:10:03.065 --> 01:10:04.874
You come here,
feeling all superior,


01:10:05.000 --> 01:10:07.981
thinking you're who knows what,
calling me a liar.


01:10:08.070 --> 01:10:11.142
I was standing there 10 years ago, talking
about love to the point of exhaustion,


01:10:11.240 --> 01:10:14.312
and you still left!


01:10:14.410 --> 01:10:17.653
You took all that with you!


01:10:17.746 --> 01:10:20.989
And I won't let you do
the same thing to me.


01:10:21.083 --> 01:10:24.189
That's what I'm doing with that kid, okay?
I'm compensating.


01:10:24.320 --> 01:10:26.300
Because life will go on
when he leaves too.


01:10:26.388 --> 01:10:28.868
And when you leave again...


01:10:49.044 --> 01:10:51.820
It was wonderful meeting everybody.
Thank you so much for dinner last night.


01:10:51.914 --> 01:10:53.791
It was beautiful. Thank you.


01:10:59.922 --> 01:11:02.562
Asher...


01:11:02.658 --> 01:11:04.968
Oh, oh, she's coming back.
She's coming back.


01:11:05.094 --> 01:11:06.767
Yep.


01:11:06.895 --> 01:11:08.875
Asher!


01:11:13.569 --> 01:11:15.048
Ash, wait!


01:11:16.305 --> 01:11:18.376
- I'm sorry.
- Oh, it's fine. It's fine.


01:11:18.474 --> 01:11:20.215
Hey, can you bring my stuff
to the hospital, please?


01:11:20.309 --> 01:11:21.754
I don't really feel like
going back inside.


01:11:21.844 --> 01:11:23.323
No, no, no. Don't leave like this.


01:11:23.445 --> 01:11:24.685
- What?
- I'm sorry.


01:11:24.780 --> 01:11:26.259
How? How do you want me to leave?


01:11:26.382 --> 01:11:27.884
- I'm sorry.
- What am I doing here?


01:11:27.983 --> 01:11:29.894
What are you sorry for? What?


01:11:33.155 --> 01:11:34.293
I slept with him.


01:11:34.423 --> 01:11:36.903
I'm sorry that I slept with him.


01:11:36.992 --> 01:11:40.940
You think that's why I'm leaving?
I know you slept with him.


01:11:41.063 --> 01:11:43.134
I knew that the moment
I saw you two together.


01:11:43.265 --> 01:11:45.108
Come on, I'm not that stupid, Clara.


01:11:45.234 --> 01:11:48.408
What? Then... what?


01:11:51.073 --> 01:11:53.383
You still think you're using me.


01:11:53.475 --> 01:11:55.113
No, Asher, I'm not...


01:11:55.244 --> 01:11:59.249
I... I know you're not, but <i>you</i> don't.


01:11:59.348 --> 01:12:01.419
And as you stand here
and say it to me,


01:12:01.517 --> 01:12:04.760
you still think you're lying to me.


01:12:04.853 --> 01:12:09.029
You think you're using me,
but actually you want me...


01:12:09.158 --> 01:12:12.628
in the same way that you think
you sleep around to keep your distance,


01:12:12.728 --> 01:12:14.833
but in fact you're looking for closeness.


01:12:14.963 --> 01:12:19.036
In the exact same way,
Clara, that you insult your patients.


01:12:19.168 --> 01:12:21.978
You think you do that
because you can't stand them?


01:12:22.071 --> 01:12:24.881
It's in fact because you adore them.


01:12:27.376 --> 01:12:30.619
You don't know yourself at all.


01:12:30.713 --> 01:12:32.158
No clue why you do anything.


01:12:38.220 --> 01:12:42.760
It'd be adorable if it wasn't so pathetic.


01:13:29.671 --> 01:13:32.151
And you left my car in Los Angeles.


01:13:39.348 --> 01:13:41.385
How have you been feeling?


01:13:41.517 --> 01:13:42.587
Fine.


01:13:44.720 --> 01:13:49.191
Lily, I wanted to apologize for what
happened at the last appointment.


01:13:49.291 --> 01:13:52.864
It was unprofessional
and I'm really sorry.


01:13:55.798 --> 01:13:57.277
I wanted to wait for Beto...


01:13:57.399 --> 01:13:59.572
Beto is not coming.


01:13:59.701 --> 01:14:02.113
- Is he working?
- No.


01:14:02.237 --> 01:14:04.444
You were right.


01:14:05.941 --> 01:14:07.750
Mm.


01:14:07.843 --> 01:14:10.380
- Lily...
- And speaking about that...


01:14:10.479 --> 01:14:12.755
since this is
our last scheduled checkup,


01:14:12.848 --> 01:14:17.263
I wanted to let you know
I'm changing my delivery plan.


01:14:17.352 --> 01:14:22.097
I respect you a lot, but I won't be
needing your services anymore.


01:14:22.191 --> 01:14:23.932
I've been talking to Dr. Malmet,


01:14:24.026 --> 01:14:28.668
and I think his energy suits mine better.


01:14:28.797 --> 01:14:32.267
Of course. It's your plan.


01:14:32.401 --> 01:14:35.939
You have to do
whatever helps you best,


01:14:36.071 --> 01:14:39.450
- and Dr. Malmet is excellent.
- Can we begin?


01:14:39.575 --> 01:14:41.577
Of course.


01:14:49.017 --> 01:14:52.089
Clara, it's me and Bobby.


01:14:55.257 --> 01:14:56.827
- Hello.
- Hi.


01:14:56.959 --> 01:14:59.462
<i>Tía</i> Clara, you look terrible.


01:15:01.964 --> 01:15:03.500
Sweetie, can you do me a huge favor?


01:15:03.632 --> 01:15:05.202
Can you please go
into your auntie's closet


01:15:05.334 --> 01:15:07.211
and find me an outfit I can borrow?


01:15:08.904 --> 01:15:10.645
Yep.


01:15:10.739 --> 01:15:12.150
Thank you.


01:15:14.576 --> 01:15:16.783
Don't start, Abby.
I'm wallowing in my grief.


01:15:16.879 --> 01:15:18.051
It's like I killed someone.


01:15:18.180 --> 01:15:21.286
You're being ridiculous.
Get up and do something.


01:15:21.383 --> 01:15:25.331
This is just self-indulgent movie crap.


01:15:25.420 --> 01:15:28.833
Okay, so things went sideways
with a couple of guys.


01:15:28.924 --> 01:15:31.837
You're an adult. Get up
and dust yourself off.


01:15:31.927 --> 01:15:33.167
That's it.


01:15:35.197 --> 01:15:36.505
What?


01:15:36.632 --> 01:15:38.475
No, it's cute that you say that to me.


01:15:38.567 --> 01:15:40.604
You've no idea
what you're talking about.


01:15:40.702 --> 01:15:43.512
- Mm-hmm.
- I envy you, sis.


01:15:43.639 --> 01:15:47.348
You don't know how it feels when you can't
breathe because someone's not there.


01:15:47.476 --> 01:15:50.548
That's the truth. You didn't get it 10
years ago, when you married Max,


01:15:50.679 --> 01:15:54.354
and you don't get it now, as you stay
with him due to a lack of imagination.


01:15:54.483 --> 01:15:55.723
Mom?


01:15:57.986 --> 01:15:59.397
I'm sorry, Bobs, I was playing.


01:15:59.521 --> 01:16:01.558
- I didn't mean... I didn't mean that.
- Let's go.


01:16:01.690 --> 01:16:03.033
- Abby, please...
- No, leave me alone.


01:16:03.158 --> 01:16:04.136
Just leave me alone!


01:16:04.226 --> 01:16:06.866
You don't even know
which guy takes your breath away.


01:16:19.575 --> 01:16:23.045
<i>This is Asher Grace.
Message, please.</i>


01:16:50.606 --> 01:16:52.085
Oh, hey, it's you!


01:16:52.207 --> 01:16:56.121
Hey... Ooh!
You brought a <i>chica!</i>


01:16:56.244 --> 01:16:59.748
Oh, my God, congratulations.
He is so sweet!


01:16:59.881 --> 01:17:01.519
Too bad he's lost in bed.


01:17:01.617 --> 01:17:04.120
I... I blame his college
girlfriends for that.


01:17:04.252 --> 01:17:05.526
Ooh.


01:17:16.365 --> 01:17:19.972
Hey, Dani, what's up?
I'm singing about you.


01:17:20.102 --> 01:17:21.843
"The First Cut ls the Deepest."


01:17:21.970 --> 01:17:24.780
It means "the first wound
is the most..."


01:17:24.873 --> 01:17:27.479
'Sup? Oh, you're bringing <i>me...</i>
I'll have one more.


01:17:27.609 --> 01:17:30.089
No, no, no. It's time to go, Claridad.


01:17:32.014 --> 01:17:33.459
Well...


01:17:33.548 --> 01:17:34.686
There we are.


01:17:34.816 --> 01:17:37.592
- Ooh.
- Here you go.


01:17:37.686 --> 01:17:39.359
Keys.


01:17:39.488 --> 01:17:41.331
Hmm.


01:17:42.557 --> 01:17:44.833
It's so unfair.


01:17:44.960 --> 01:17:46.303
What is?


01:17:46.395 --> 01:17:48.375
I used to dream about this.


01:17:50.165 --> 01:17:51.371
What, about this?


01:17:53.068 --> 01:17:56.174
Yeah, I'd be with a guy in a bar,


01:17:56.304 --> 01:17:58.648
and you showed up and carried me out.


01:18:01.743 --> 01:18:03.518
What's unfair about it?


01:18:05.714 --> 01:18:08.285
My dream wasn't sad.


01:18:11.953 --> 01:18:14.433
Come on.


01:18:33.208 --> 01:18:35.518
What?


01:18:35.644 --> 01:18:38.124
What is it?


01:18:45.153 --> 01:18:48.157
Can you breathe
when you're not with me?


01:18:48.256 --> 01:18:51.863
What? I...


01:18:51.993 --> 01:18:54.473
Yes.


01:19:02.037 --> 01:19:05.018
Do you think we've ever been <i>in love?</i>


01:19:07.175 --> 01:19:08.654
Oh, my... All right.


01:19:08.744 --> 01:19:10.348
Okay, your sister is an imbecile.


01:19:10.445 --> 01:19:11.856
No, it's not about her.


01:19:11.947 --> 01:19:13.551
I know. It...


01:19:16.551 --> 01:19:18.030
It's about this.


01:19:20.155 --> 01:19:21.395
This wasn't here two months ago.


01:19:21.490 --> 01:19:23.527
Because I'm getting old!


01:19:23.625 --> 01:19:25.730
This is an old lady hand freckle!


01:19:25.827 --> 01:19:27.101
You're not helping.


01:19:27.229 --> 01:19:29.800
I'm saying that it's new.


01:19:32.300 --> 01:19:36.771
I know every inch of you,
but you remain surprising.


01:19:36.905 --> 01:19:42.048
I notice every tiny change
because I'm here to notice.


01:19:43.612 --> 01:19:46.149
My purpose in life...


01:19:47.783 --> 01:19:51.424
is to keep track of you,
Abigail Barron.


01:19:51.520 --> 01:19:55.434
And I don't...
care what your family theory is,


01:19:55.524 --> 01:19:59.904
and I am sure that it is complex,
but that's love.


01:20:06.034 --> 01:20:09.015
I can breathe without you just fine.


01:20:11.206 --> 01:20:13.311
What would be the point?


01:20:24.753 --> 01:20:27.791
Thank you for running my bath
like an English butler.


01:20:27.923 --> 01:20:30.130
Don't mention it.


01:20:30.258 --> 01:20:35.105
I had a good look
when you went in, so... we both won.


01:20:38.767 --> 01:20:40.769
Can I ask you a serious question?


01:20:40.869 --> 01:20:43.110
Mm-hmm.


01:20:45.373 --> 01:20:47.353
Are you leaving again?


01:20:50.278 --> 01:20:51.814
I don't know.


01:20:53.281 --> 01:20:55.761
Why'd you come back?


01:20:55.851 --> 01:20:56.921
Don't say it was because of us,


01:20:57.018 --> 01:20:59.294
because you spent months here
without a word.


01:21:08.396 --> 01:21:10.171
I'm no longer
with Doctors Without Borders.


01:21:11.633 --> 01:21:13.306
Why?


01:21:13.401 --> 01:21:15.813
Because...


01:21:15.904 --> 01:21:18.248
they very kindly asked me to leave,


01:21:18.373 --> 01:21:20.319
as it seemed...


01:21:22.677 --> 01:21:24.486
I was not committed.


01:21:28.950 --> 01:21:31.191
They know you.


01:21:31.286 --> 01:21:33.163
Yeah.


01:21:38.193 --> 01:21:41.436
So you came back because you have
nowhere far to be.


01:21:45.433 --> 01:21:46.912
That's horrible.


01:21:50.805 --> 01:21:53.615
I mean, all my life I've wanted to be
elsewhere.


01:21:55.911 --> 01:21:58.790
Your neck is the only thing
that called me back...


01:21:58.914 --> 01:22:00.916
And my Mom's cooking.


01:22:01.049 --> 01:22:02.084
That too.


01:22:04.319 --> 01:22:06.595
But the truth is...


01:22:06.721 --> 01:22:11.431
that most of the time
I just want to go to hell.


01:22:15.230 --> 01:22:17.710
The food's terrible there.


01:22:24.472 --> 01:22:26.577
I don't want to go there with you.


01:22:31.246 --> 01:22:33.692
Well, then I'll go on my own.


01:22:35.717 --> 01:22:39.028
Just don't say I didn't ask you
to come, okay?


01:23:21.229 --> 01:23:23.175
Are you in love with him?


01:23:26.301 --> 01:23:28.144
Mom, I've always been in love with him.


01:23:28.236 --> 01:23:33.652
Well, he's family.
You love him like he's family.


01:23:33.742 --> 01:23:36.450
But that doesn't mean
you're <i>in love</i> with him.


01:23:39.581 --> 01:23:41.151
Ever since he left...


01:23:42.817 --> 01:23:44.956
I've measured all guys against him.


01:23:45.053 --> 01:23:49.331
Well, not against him,
but against what he... made me feel.


01:23:49.424 --> 01:23:51.995
And they were no match,
and I loved getting rid of them.


01:23:52.093 --> 01:23:53.629
It made me feel superior.


01:23:53.728 --> 01:23:55.571
It made me feel
like I'd avoided a mistake,


01:23:55.697 --> 01:23:57.142
so I wouldn't settle and become...


01:23:57.232 --> 01:23:58.506
Your sister.


01:24:00.935 --> 01:24:02.573
Yeah.


01:24:05.340 --> 01:24:07.581
That's a horrible way of thinking, right?


01:24:10.278 --> 01:24:13.725
Meanwhile, you and Dad...


01:24:13.848 --> 01:24:17.694
you make a big show of your wedding,


01:24:17.786 --> 01:24:20.392
like we needed to feel
even less than we do.


01:24:20.522 --> 01:24:22.331
Oh, nonsense!


01:24:22.424 --> 01:24:25.701
It's the truth, Mom.
You two set an impossible example.


01:24:25.827 --> 01:24:27.864
Don't be dumb, honey.


01:24:27.996 --> 01:24:30.306
You know how many times
I've fallen out of love with your Dad?


01:24:30.398 --> 01:24:32.537
I've lost count.


01:24:32.667 --> 01:24:36.740
Besides, do you think when we got
together we knew we'd be this lucky?


01:24:36.871 --> 01:24:39.408
When I met your Dad,


01:24:39.541 --> 01:24:44.012
he was a barefoot wetback painting
graffiti around Echo Park.


01:24:44.112 --> 01:24:47.025
I moved in with him because...


01:24:47.115 --> 01:24:50.722
he was the most handsome man
I'd ever seen. That's the truth.


01:24:51.853 --> 01:24:55.824
But do you think I ever thought
I'd marry him 40 years later,


01:24:55.924 --> 01:24:58.427
more in love with him than ever?


01:24:58.560 --> 01:25:01.063
Things didn't look
very promising back then.


01:25:01.196 --> 01:25:05.110
You see? Then nobody knows anything
and the whole thing is a scam.


01:25:05.233 --> 01:25:07.042
No, it's not a scam , baby.


01:25:07.135 --> 01:25:10.412
Everybody ends up loving somebody.


01:25:10.538 --> 01:25:13.576
But it's pure chance.


01:25:13.708 --> 01:25:17.087
You meet somebody,
and you bet on them,


01:25:17.212 --> 01:25:19.590
with no guarantees.


01:25:19.714 --> 01:25:21.193
And if you ask me,


01:25:21.282 --> 01:25:26.061
you already have the advantage of knowing
on whom you want to bet.


01:25:26.154 --> 01:25:29.397
- Mom...
- Love doesn't have to be simple, baby.


01:25:31.192 --> 01:25:33.138
But it does have to be easy.


01:25:42.937 --> 01:25:46.578
Mom, you're a witch.


01:25:46.674 --> 01:25:48.620
Hello?


01:25:48.710 --> 01:25:50.280
<i>Hi, Dr. Barron?</i>


01:25:50.378 --> 01:25:52.984
Dr... Barron? Asher.


01:25:53.114 --> 01:25:54.821
I'm calling about Lily Alvarez.


01:25:54.949 --> 01:25:56.485
<i>What's going on?</i>


01:25:56.618 --> 01:25:59.963
Look, Clara, she's, uh...


01:26:00.054 --> 01:26:03.092
She's gone into labor,
and she's all by herself.


01:26:03.191 --> 01:26:05.637
<i>Now, I know you're not
her doctor anymore,</i>


01:26:05.727 --> 01:26:07.673
but she's terrified,
and since you broke up her marriage,


01:26:07.795 --> 01:26:09.502
- I thought maybe...
- I'll be right there.


01:26:13.468 --> 01:26:15.141
If everybody loves somebody,
I love <i>you.</i>


01:26:15.236 --> 01:26:16.874
Mm!


01:26:17.005 --> 01:26:20.646
Who'd have told me
you'd be my cheesy daughter?


01:26:30.785 --> 01:26:31.855
Hi, Beto.


01:26:31.986 --> 01:26:33.090
Beto, Beto, Beto.


01:26:33.188 --> 01:26:34.667
No, get dressed.
You can't come looking like that.


01:26:34.789 --> 01:26:36.496
Your wife is about to give birth.


01:26:36.624 --> 01:26:39.332
Yeah, I know, but she
doesn't want me there.


01:26:39.460 --> 01:26:41.872
Oh, my God, Beto! Okay.


01:26:41.996 --> 01:26:43.304
I don't wanna tell you what to do,


01:26:43.398 --> 01:26:45.810
because last time you listened to me
it was a huge mess,


01:26:45.900 --> 01:26:47.140
but here it goes...


01:26:47.235 --> 01:26:49.442
Your issue with Lily
is you listen to her too much.


01:26:49.537 --> 01:26:50.880
She's your wife, she's in labor,


01:26:51.005 --> 01:26:53.178
and you'll be there...
whether she likes it or not.


01:26:53.308 --> 01:26:55.345
Okay?


01:26:55.476 --> 01:26:57.888
She'll like it. You'll see.


01:26:58.012 --> 01:27:00.492
Yeah, yeah...
I'm coming, I'm coming.


01:27:14.596 --> 01:27:17.736
Beto! Beto! Beto...


01:27:17.865 --> 01:27:19.538
See? Told you.


01:27:19.667 --> 01:27:21.704
Oh, Beto...


01:27:21.836 --> 01:27:25.181
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.


01:27:25.273 --> 01:27:28.049
No, I am sorry.
I should've been here earlier.


01:27:28.176 --> 01:27:30.087
Way earlier...


01:27:31.112 --> 01:27:33.456
Hi. I'm Dr. Barron.


01:27:33.581 --> 01:27:36.790
I'm here to check up
on Clark Alvarez's cleaning.


01:27:36.918 --> 01:27:39.694
Sure. I was about
to bring him to his parents.


01:27:39.787 --> 01:27:41.130
Oh, that's okay. I'll do it.


01:27:41.256 --> 01:27:44.135
- Okay. You're welcome.
- Thanks.


01:27:44.259 --> 01:27:47.570
He's named after Superman.


01:27:55.737 --> 01:27:57.273
Hey.


01:28:03.411 --> 01:28:06.392
- Hi.
- Hey.


01:28:08.816 --> 01:28:10.727
It's good that you came.


01:28:10.818 --> 01:28:12.593
Can't believe you brought Beto.


01:28:12.687 --> 01:28:17.329
Yeah, turns out I miss the Alvarezes.
Who would've thought?


01:28:17.458 --> 01:28:18.766
Me.


01:28:22.263 --> 01:28:24.334
Never know what you have, right?


01:28:35.276 --> 01:28:36.254
I should go.


01:28:36.344 --> 01:28:37.322
Ahem.


01:28:37.445 --> 01:28:40.915
Okay, uh, good to see you, Dr. Grace.


01:28:41.015 --> 01:28:43.256
Goodbye, Dr. Barron.


01:28:58.599 --> 01:29:04.345
Look, Clark, those are your parents.


01:29:04.472 --> 01:29:07.476
We'll have a long chat
about them later, okay?


01:29:07.608 --> 01:29:10.088
I know.


01:29:15.817 --> 01:29:17.819
Here he is.


01:29:20.822 --> 01:29:24.998
Hi, Clark...


01:29:25.126 --> 01:29:28.539
What's up, son?


01:29:28.663 --> 01:29:30.301
What's up, baby?


01:29:30.398 --> 01:29:32.309
<i>Ay, ay, ay, ay, ay...</i>


01:29:32.400 --> 01:29:34.311
Are you calmer now?


01:29:36.571 --> 01:29:38.016
What happened, my boy?


01:29:38.106 --> 01:29:40.143
You'll make him cry. Give him to me.


01:29:40.241 --> 01:29:42.243
No, he's fine. He's fine with his Dad.


01:29:42.377 --> 01:29:44.254
- You're holding him wrong.
- No, baby, like this.


01:29:55.556 --> 01:29:57.536
- Just taste it.
- Okay, okay, okay.


01:30:01.429 --> 01:30:03.375
Is it good?


01:30:03.464 --> 01:30:06.035
Uh-huh. Ahem. Yeah.


01:30:10.037 --> 01:30:13.280
What you doing that for?


01:30:13.408 --> 01:30:15.684
Bobby, don't answer that alone!


01:30:15.777 --> 01:30:18.257
It's Aunt Clara. I told her to wait.


01:30:23.918 --> 01:30:25.864
I was...


01:30:25.953 --> 01:30:28.058
Don't apologize.


01:30:28.156 --> 01:30:30.932
- You were wrong.
- I know.


01:30:31.058 --> 01:30:33.561
No, I'm not saying you were wrong
in what you said.


01:30:33.661 --> 01:30:35.766
I mean you're <i>wrong,</i>


01:30:35.897 --> 01:30:38.377
fundamentally wrong about my marriage.


01:30:40.368 --> 01:30:41.904
I know.


01:30:42.036 --> 01:30:44.346
I really do.


01:30:44.439 --> 01:30:47.181
Okay.


01:30:54.882 --> 01:30:57.260
What are you doing over there?


01:30:57.385 --> 01:30:59.387
- Well...
- There's pasta.


01:31:03.491 --> 01:31:05.027
Fine. We forgive you.


01:31:19.574 --> 01:31:23.044
- So, pasta, huh?
- Yeah. I made the sauce.


01:31:23.144 --> 01:31:25.624
You literally just got here. Don't.


01:31:36.257 --> 01:31:37.964
Mm!


01:31:38.092 --> 01:31:39.662
- You look so good.
- Hmm!


01:31:39.794 --> 01:31:41.637
You look happy.


01:31:41.729 --> 01:31:44.437
See, I had like a thousand epiphanies.


01:31:44.532 --> 01:31:46.273
Yuck! That's why I avoid them
at all costs.


01:31:49.303 --> 01:31:51.943
My patients had their baby
yesterday and I saw them...


01:31:52.039 --> 01:31:55.179
Well, it was the patients
with the serious issues...


01:31:55.309 --> 01:31:56.811
The mole patients?


01:31:56.911 --> 01:31:58.322
Yeah, those patients.


01:31:58.412 --> 01:32:02.827
They were holding their baby
and all I could think of was...


01:32:02.917 --> 01:32:04.658
"I want that."


01:32:04.752 --> 01:32:07.665
You want to argue?
I can help you there.


01:32:09.257 --> 01:32:13.000
I see it all the time: new babies,
happy couples, families.


01:32:13.094 --> 01:32:15.335
But I want that now.


01:32:18.165 --> 01:32:20.645
- I know...
- No, you and I are family.


01:32:20.735 --> 01:32:23.716
We're no longer a couple.
We grew past that.


01:32:23.838 --> 01:32:25.545
I know, I know...


01:32:27.775 --> 01:32:29.686
I'm sorry about the way I left, okay?


01:32:33.848 --> 01:32:36.385
I'm sorry I let you go.


01:32:36.517 --> 01:32:38.724
The number-one thing I always tell
girls your age


01:32:38.853 --> 01:32:40.355
is always, always use a condom.


01:32:40.454 --> 01:32:42.127
The fact that you
have already had a kid


01:32:42.223 --> 01:32:45.295
and in a month you already look
like that is <i>amazing!</i>


01:32:45.393 --> 01:32:49.364
Face just hit the surfboard,
and I started, just, like...


01:32:49.497 --> 01:32:52.307
<i>Love. I see it every day.</i>


01:32:54.168 --> 01:32:56.375
Come on!


01:32:56.504 --> 01:32:58.984
<i>And everybody has it.</i>


01:33:09.350 --> 01:33:11.830
<i>It doesn't matter if it doesn't
look like what you imagined.</i>


01:33:20.394 --> 01:33:22.772
Guys, I love you.


01:33:22.897 --> 01:33:25.776
<i>Or if it’s not fed every day...</i>


01:33:25.900 --> 01:33:29.905
- Don't be a stranger.
- No, no, no. I'll be back soon.


01:33:30.938 --> 01:33:32.178
Thank you.


01:33:36.544 --> 01:33:40.014
<i>Or if it changes and is reborn.</i>


01:33:40.114 --> 01:33:41.593
Mmm!


01:33:46.921 --> 01:33:48.264
Love you, guys!


01:33:48.356 --> 01:33:50.597
<i>Nobody knows anything.</i>


01:33:50.691 --> 01:33:54.138
<i>I do believe that love is ridiculous,
complicated and unlikely.</i>


01:33:57.932 --> 01:33:57.941
<i>But we have to let it be.</i>


01:33:57.965 --> 01:34:00.571
<i>But we have to let it be.</i>


01:34:00.668 --> 01:34:03.979
<i>It surprises you when you least expect it.</i>


01:34:15.616 --> 01:34:17.618
First date, Grace.


01:34:19.020 --> 01:34:21.500
Tablecloths.


01:34:41.542 --> 01:34:44.022
Hmm.


01:35:07.201 --> 01:35:08.339
Asher...


01:35:08.469 --> 01:35:10.176
I... I don't need a big speech,


01:35:10.304 --> 01:35:12.341
and you clearly don't know
very much, anyway.


01:35:12.473 --> 01:35:15.113
That was the gist of my speech!


01:35:20.181 --> 01:35:23.060
You know, you don't know
everything, either.


01:35:23.184 --> 01:35:25.391
Yeah, I know that, too.


01:35:25.519 --> 01:35:27.294
Mm!


01:35:32.660 --> 01:35:33.638
Oh!


01:35:33.728 --> 01:35:35.730
I still got you there!
Have to catch me!


01:35:40.868 --> 01:35:41.903
Ahem.


01:35:43.504 --> 01:35:46.178
Australian Asher Grace is back.


01:35:48.042 --> 01:35:51.023
- Pay up. Money. Give it to me.
- Pay him.


01:35:51.112 --> 01:35:53.251
This was a bet?
When did this become a bet?


01:35:53.380 --> 01:35:55.018
- That's...
- That's the way we are.


01:35:55.116 --> 01:35:56.288
You bet against me!


01:35:56.417 --> 01:35:58.727
Just for the record, I'd like you to see
who's collecting the money.


01:35:58.819 --> 01:36:01.390
Yeah, well, thank you, Max, but...


01:36:01.489 --> 01:36:03.366
Don't come to me with your dollar.

										
   
 

  


 

  



  
  
 

 										
